      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Phrases are coherent melodic units, usually 4 or 8 bars, ending with cadences."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "grouping",
      "title": "Grouping",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Irish dance tunes: two-bar cells → eight-bar parts. Songs: antecedent (question) + consequent (answer) phrases."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "harmonic-rhythm",
      "title": "Harmonic rhythm",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "How often chords change shapes feel. One chord per bar vs one chord for four bars creates different energy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "analysis-skill",
      "title": "Analysis skill",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Map phrases to find breathe points, variation spots, and percussion turns."
        }
      ]
    }
